       The  ooppeennaatt22()  system call is an extension of ooppeennaatt(2) and provides a
       superset of its functionality.

       The ooppeennaatt22() system call opens the file specified  by  _p_a_t_h.   If  the
       specified  file does not exist, it may optionally (if OO__CCRREEAATT is speci‐
       fied in _h_o_w_._f_l_a_g_s) be created.

       As with ooppeennaatt(2), if _p_a_t_h is relative, then it is interpreted relative
       to the directory referred to by the file descriptor _d_i_r_f_d (or the  cur‐
       rent  working directory of the calling process, if _d_i_r_f_d is the special
       value AATT__FFDDCCWWDD).  If _p_a_t_h is absolute, then _d_i_r_f_d  is  ignored  (unless
       _h_o_w_._r_e_s_o_l_v_e  contains  RREESSOOLLVVEE__IINN__RROOOOTT,  in which case _p_a_t_h is resolved
       relative to _d_i_r_f_d).

       Rather than taking a single _f_l_a_g_s  argument,  an  extensible  structure
       (_h_o_w) is passed to allow for future extensions.  The _s_i_z_e argument must
       be specified as _s_i_z_e_o_f_(_s_t_r_u_c_t _o_p_e_n___h_o_w_).

