       perset  of the _f_l_a_g_s and _m_o_d_e arguments to ooppeennaatt(2).  This argument is
       a pointer to an _o_p_e_n___h_o_w structure, described in ooppeenn__hhooww(2type).

       Any future extensions to ooppeennaatt22() will be implemented  as  new  fields
       appended  to  the  _o_p_e_n___h_o_w structure, with a zero value in a new field
       resulting in the kernel behaving as though that extension field was not
       present.  Therefore, the caller _m_u_s_t zero‐fill this structure  on  ini‐
       tialization.   (See  the  "Extensibility" section of the NNOOTTEESS for more
       detail on why this is necessary.)

